#### 5. Competitor Analysis & Fact-Check Summary
* **Competitor URL:** Blank in source row (no competitor URL invented).
* **Factual Standards Verified & Cited:**
  * **BIS Hallmarking & HUID:** Verified that under mandatory Bureau of Indian Standards regulations, newly crafted antique-finish gold jewellery sold in India must bear the 3-mark BIS hallmark (BIS triangular logo, purity/fineness grade like 22K916 or 18K750, and 6-digit alphanumeric HUID verifiable on the official BIS CARE App). Antique oxidation/patina does not exempt modern jewellery from hallmarking.
  * **Purity Differences:** 22K (91.6% fineness) allows deep hand-chisel relief for traditional temple Nakshi carving; 18K (75.0% fineness) provides superior tensile strength and prong security for diamond-accented and flexible link sets.
  * **Making Charges & Weight Accounting:** Art-intensive Nakshi repoussé work commands higher making charges (12% to 25%+). Non-gold materials (kemp stones, polki, pearls, lac) must be deducted from gross weight, billing gold strictly on net gold weight.
  * **GST Rate:** 3% GST under HSN 7113 applied to gold value, stones, and making charges.
  * **Care Rules:** Strictly dry cleaning with microfibre cloth and soft camel-hair brush; chemical cleaners and ultrasonic baths prohibited as they dissolve the specialized surface patina.

